<article class="env-proposition" id="040C">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/040C">Proposition <span data-tag="040C">8.5.4.11</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category. The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(1)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is idempotent-complete. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(2)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ admits limits indexed by $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{Idem})$. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(3)$</dt>
<dd><p>
The $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ admits colimits indexed by $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{Idem})$. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is an immediate consequence of Corollary <a data-tag="0403" href="/tag/0403">8.5.3.11</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
